{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sarcastic-rusted-akitainu","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe rolling 5-of-10 breaker counts low-level noise and cannot distinguish an exhausted logical operation from its physical attempts. The approved replacement must stop only demonstrably unhealthy scopes without terminating work that historical jobs completed.\n\n## Outcome\nImplement an endpoint/provider finite-pass fuse over normalized coordinator outcomes. Endpoint opens after three consecutive eligible exhausted logical outcomes across at least two tickets; provider additionally requires two endpoint families. Matching success resets consecutive state.\n\n## Plan\n1. Count only exhausted logical outcomes eligible under the failure policy. Never count physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404s, or opaque diagnostic text.\n2. Track endpoint consecutive outcomes and distinct tickets. Track provider scope only when failures span two endpoint families.\n3. Reset matching consecutive state on success; independent scopes retain their own state and continue.\n4. Preserve direct authoritative credential, configuration, quota, rate, issue, endpoint, tenant, provider, and global stop/defer behavior without inferring scope from text.\n5. When open, return explicit scope/reason/`retry_not_before` metadata; do not execute matching remaining plans.\n\n## Testing\nSequence tables pin threshold boundaries, exclusions, reset, two-ticket/two-family requirements, and independent scopes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Endpoint fuse opens only after three consecutive eligible exhausted outcomes across at least two tickets.\n- [ ] Provider fuse additionally requires two endpoint families.\n- [ ] A matching success resets the consecutive state.\n- [ ] Physical attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, ticket-local 404s, and opaque diagnostics never increment inferred counters.\n- [ ] Independent scopes continue when another scope opens.\n- [ ] Open-fuse outcomes include exact scope, reason, and `retry_not_before`.\n\n## Out of scope\nProduction routing, batch tallies, and historical replay integration.","id":"dd65-54fa-f4c3-4bc9","parent_id":"28a3-a62d-6345-44a0","priority":1,"tags":["rp03","fuse","retry","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S3 T2 — Implement the scoped finite-pass fuse"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787028210057535001,"uuid":"4ecdda90-bf70-4227-b9bc-1af55f7d7b20"}